From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Carney <dcarney@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 14:57:20 +0000
Subject: Track external memory separately from the global allocation limit

Upstream V8 14.8 removed the external_memory_accounted_in_global_limit
flag (commits 6a5039d9db92 and cf511a65adc5), hardcoding the behavior
where external memory is always accounted in the global allocation limit.

This is problematic for workerd because:
- Workers have tight 128MB heap limits
- Folding external memory into global limits causes double-counting
  and overly aggressive GC triggering
- The old soft/hard limit mechanism in HandleExternalMemoryInterrupt()
  provided better graduated GC responses for our use case

Rather than restoring the removed flag, this patch hardcodes the
flag-disabled (false) behavior directly: external memory is tracked
separately via HandleExternalMemoryInterrupt() with soft/hard limit
thresholds, and is excluded from the global allocation limit
computations. This keeps the patch minimal by dropping the now-unused
flag and all of its conditional branches.

Co-authored-by: Divy Srivastava <divy@cloudflare.com>

